            body: "Safe Surrey made 26 trackable promises and costed none of them; three carry dates, and the rest depend on money, the Province, or TransLink that the party has not secured. With eight of nine votes, there is no one else to blame when a line slips.\n\n### The biggest tickets\n\nA full-service hospital on City land, SkyTrain to Newton, three new pools or aquatic centres plus a Newton community centre, a police helicopter and drone fleet, and four years of 0% property tax to pay for all of it. McCallum declined to give costs at the hospital launch and said the savings would come from inside City Hall.\n\n### The first deadlines\n\nA forensic auditor engaged as a \"first act\" after the early-November inaugural meeting; Elections BC filings by January 15, 2027; the helicopter and drones in the air by early February 2027; and the 2027 financial plan, due by May 15, 2027, where 0% meets the police budget.\n\n### What to watch at the first meetings\n\nWhether the auditor is independent and the scope covers the arena land exchange and 7580 152 Street; whether the Metro Vancouver withdrawal starts with a letter to the Province or with the study they swore off; how many items go in camera after a promise of none; and whether the first budget moves the parcel tax, utility rates, or recreation fees while the property tax line stays at zero.",
