            body: "The helicopter window runs 90 days from the inaugural meeting, Elections BC filings fall due 90 days after voting day, each financial plan must be adopted by May 15, and the next election is Saturday, October 19, 2030.\n\n- **Inaugural council meeting**: November 2, 2026 (Estimated; the 2022 inaugural was November 7)\n- **Elections BC filings due**: January 15, 2027 (90 days after voting day)\n- **Helicopter and drones: 90 days**: January 31 to February 7, 2027 (90 days from the inaugural meeting)\n- **Budget 2027: the first 0% test**: March 1 to May 15, 2027\n- **Budget 2028**: March 1 to May 15, 2028\n- **Budget 2029**: March 1 to May 15, 2029\n- **Budget 2030**: March 1 to May 15, 2030\n- **Next election**: October 19, 2030\n\nA promise is scored against what the party said, not against what is reasonable; where a pledge collides with provincial law, the collision is noted so \"the Province wouldn't let us\" can be judged on its own terms.",
