            title: "Announcements",
            body: "Every dated release and event behind the promises above, newest first. New commitments are added as the council makes them.\n\n### Election night, Bombay Banquet Hall\n\n*Oct 17, 2026*\n\n\"We will address your safety and we will address your infrastructure\"; no specific commitments; McCallum tells the room Nagra will be deputy mayor\n\nSources: [Peace Arch News, Oct 17, 2026](https://surreynowleader.com/2026/10/17/surrey-mayral-race-doug-mccallum-topples-brenda-locke-to-win-5th-term/) · [Voice, Oct 17, 2026](https://voiceonline.com/mccallum-will-be-mayor-of-surrey-for-third-time-says-nagra-will-be-deputy-mayor-updates/)\n\n### Candidate questionnaires, Surrey Now-Leader\n\n*Oct 4, 2026*\n\nMcCallum: 0% taxes, hospital, helicopter and drones in 90 days, recreation fee freeze, free swim lessons, free senior pool access, Farm Local; claims Locke cut $47 million from the police request, raised taxes nearly 30% in four years, and spent $150 million fighting Victoria. Elford: $10,000 dumping fines and 10-year bans. Patton: heritage west of 140 Street, no-tree-cut bylaw, stop the 89-townhome project. Cloke and Patton: Rosemary Heights as park. Guerra: Cloverdale pool. Suhana Gill: swim lessons ages three to 16, City Centre pool and community centre\n\nSources: [Candidate index, Oct 4, 2026](https://surreynowleader.com/2026/10/04/surrey-votes-meet-your-candidates-for-mayor-council-school-board/)\n\n### Release: a Safe Surrey council will bring back wards\n\n*Oct 2, 2026*\n\nEight wards of similar population, drawn by an independent commission; council adopts a ward bylaw; Province asked to approve; \"one name and one phone number\" per area\n\nSources: [Cloverdale Reporter, Oct 2, 2026](https://cloverdalereporter.com/2026/10/02/mccallum-says-ssc-led-surrey-council-would-bring-wards-back/)\n\n### Hospital press conference at 6965 King George Boulevard\n\n*Sept 21, 2026*\n\nDonate the City land to the Province, every approval and permit within 60 days, seek provincial and federal money; \"we're not right now giving the costs\"; had not yet spoken to the Province\n\nSources: [Surrey Citizen, Sept 21, 2026](https://surreycitizen.com/mccallum-pledges-to-get-new-surrey-hospital-built-but-has-few-details/)\n\n### Cheney Cloke, former Police Board vice chair, joins the slate\n\n*Aug 4, 2026*\n\nNo new commitments\n\nSources: [Surrey Citizen, Aug 4, 2026](https://surreycitizen.com/surrey-candidate-quits-party-joins-mccallums-coalition/)\n\n### Complaints to Elections BC and the RCMP alleging India-linked Facebook pages favoured Locke\n\n*July 28 to 29, 2026*\n\nNo commitments; Elections BC found no apparent advertising violation\n\nSources: [Surrey Now-Leader, July 29, 2026](https://surreynowleader.com/2026/07/29/mccallum-files-formal-complaint-with-elections-bc-rcmp-for-claims-of-election-interference-in-surrey/)\n\n### Slate event at 99 South Vineyards, South Surrey\n\n*July 22, 2026*\n\n0% taxes four years; permits in 60 days or fees waived; forensic audit as a first act; leave Metro Vancouver except water, sewer, and waste, with no studies or task force; waive business licence fees two years; Farm Local; pools for Clayton Heights and City Centre; Newton community centre with pool; heritage for Crescent Beach and Ocean Park; no more in-camera meetings\n\nSources: [Peace Arch News, July 23, 2026](https://cloverdalereporter.com/2026/07/23/mccallum-makes-impressive-promises-at-surrey-election-campaign-event/) · [Surrey Citizen, July 23, 2026](https://surreycitizen.com/mccallum-would-pull-surrey-out-of-metro-vancouver-if-elected/) · [Daily Hive, July 22, 2026](https://dailyhive.com/vancouver/surrey-doug-mccallum-leave-metro-vancouver)\n\n### Launch at Crescent Beach with Nagra and Elford\n\n*Apr 13, 2026*\n\nSkyTrain to Newton; zero tolerance and more police; helicopter within 90 days; Clayton Heights pool; heritage zones; 0% taxes four years; Surrey Centre Opportunity Zone; a \"global city\" modelled on Dubai, New York, and London; slogan \"Doug Gets It Done\"\n\nSources: [Daily Hive, Apr 13, 2026](https://dailyhive.com/vancouver/doug-mccallum-surrey-2026) · [Voice, Apr 13, 2026](https://voiceonline.com/safe-surrey-coalition-doug-mccallum-announces-re-election-bid-vows-to-deliver-surreys-defining-legacy/) · [Surrey Now-Leader, Apr 13, 2026](https://surreynowleader.com/2026/04/13/former-surrey-mayor-doug-mccallum-running-again/)",
